You must consult the supervisory authority prior to starting the processing activities [GDPR, Recital 94, Article 36(1)].

When consulting the supervisory authority, you must provide it with the following information:
* The respective responsibilities of the controller, joint controllers, and processors involved in the processing, particularly within a group of undertakings (where applicable) [GDPR, Article 36(3)(a)];
* The purposes and means of the intended processing [GDPR, Article 36(3)(b)];
* The measures and safeguards provided to protect the rights and freedoms of data subjects pursuant to the GDPR [GDPR, Article 36(3)(c)];
* The contact details of the data protection officer (where applicable) [GDPR, Article 36(3)(d)];
* The data protection impact assessment required under Article 35 [GDPR, Article 36(3)(e)]; and
* Any other information requested by the supervisory authority [GDPR, Article 36(3)(f)].

